INT. MOVING VAN - NIGHT

Dark. The cargo hold. Boxes, stacked. A single dome light, flickering.

KIM and KIP crouch among the crates, breath fogging. Rain on the roof. A drum.

Tick. Tick.

KIP
You hear that?

KIM
Its the engine.

KIP
Not the engine.

Silence.

Something under the floor. A scrape. Slow.

KIM
Mo said the vault was empty. Mo said nobody's in the back.

Dripping. Somewhere behind the boxes.

KIP
Kim. Look at the lock.

The rear door latch. Turning. By itself.

Nothing. Then a long metal groan.

MO, 50s, soaked, gray stubble, a crowbar in one hand and a flashlight in the other, steps through the opening into the dome light, grinning like a man whos won something.

MO
Told you I'd catch up. Miss me?

Kim and Kip look at each other. Neither moves.

KIM
Mo is up front. Driving.

Mo's grin stays. The scraping starts again, from his side of the van.

Black.
